-- title:
--   A successful choice as a section of the base-graph projection
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a choice system on $t$ indices, with finite domains $D_i$ ($i\in[t]=\{0,\dots,t-1\}$), label sets $L_{ij}$ and label maps $\lambda^{\mathrm L}_{ij}\colon D_i\to L_{ij}$, $\lambda^{\mathrm R}_{ij}\colon D_j\to L_{ij}$ for $i<j$. The base graph $G_C$ is the simple graph generated by the following arcs, for all $i<j$ and every helper $h=h_{ij;\ell}$ ($\ell\notin\{i,j\}$):
--
--   - $(i,d)$ to $(j,e)$ whenever $\lambda^{\mathrm L}_{ij}(d)=\lambda^{\mathrm R}_{ij}(e)$;
--   - $(h,\lambda^{\mathrm L}_{ij}(d))$ to $(i,d)$ and $(h,\lambda^{\mathrm R}_{ij}(e))$ to $(j,e)$, for $d\in D_i$, $e\in D_j$;
--   - $(h,q)$ to $(\ell,f)$ for all $q\in L_{ij}$ and $f\in D_\ell$.
--
--   The type map $\tau\colon G_C\to T_t$ to the template forgets the second coordinate.
--
--   1. **Arcs are edges.** Every generating arc projects under $\tau$ to an edge of $T_t$; in particular its endpoints are distinct, so it is an edge of $G_C$.
--   2. **The choice map.** Let $d=(d_i)_{i\in[t]}\in\prod_i D_i$ satisfy $\lambda^{\mathrm L}_{ij}(d_i)=\lambda^{\mathrm R}_{ij}(d_j)$ for all $i<j$, i.e. be a successful choice. The map $\sigma_d\colon V(T_t)\to V(G_C)$ given by
--   $$
--   \sigma_d(i)=(i,d_i),\qquad \sigma_d(h_{ij;\ell})=\bigl(h_{ij;\ell},\ \lambda^{\mathrm L}_{ij}(d_i)\bigr)
--   $$
--   is a graph homomorphism $T_t\to G_C$, and it is a section of the type map:
--   $$
--   \tau\circ\sigma_d=\mathrm{id}_{V(T_t)} .
--   $$
--
--   The choice map is the positive half of the parity-lift reduction: a successful choice places a copy of the template inside the base graph, lying over the identity of $T_t$. On this copy, vertex weight $1$ everywhere and edge weight $1$ on exactly the edges of $T_t$ form a weighted witness for the star parity (each vertex of $T_t$ has exactly one neighbour of each adjacent type, and exactly one vertex is the main vertex $0$). This is how a successful choice yields, for $t\ge1$, the strict gap $\hom(T_t,X_\star)<\hom(T_t,X_0)$ between the star lift $X_\star$ (parity $1$ exactly at the main vertex $0$) and the zero lift $X_0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `BaseArc.type_adj` and `BaseArc.adj` are item 1; `choiceMap d hd` is $\sigma_d$, and `choiceMap_type` states that `baseType` composed with it is the identity. A section reserved for the converse direction contains no declarations.
